WEBVTT

00:06.423 --> 00:09.509
We've arrived! We've arrived!

00:10.218 --> 00:11.469
Work hard.

00:15.974 --> 00:17.642
I can't take it anymore.

00:19.269 --> 00:20.729
What are you saying?

00:20.812 --> 00:24.816
If you can't do this,
you'll get eaten by demons in no time.

00:26.484 --> 00:27.861
Tokito.

00:39.539 --> 00:43.960
Imagine this is real combat,
you've already died three times.

00:45.378 --> 00:48.923
To you who is ignorant of
What eternity means

00:49.007 --> 00:52.218
It's time to show you the answer

00:52.302 --> 00:58.600
Beyond the endless spiral

01:07.192 --> 01:12.113
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA:
HASHIRA TRAINING ARC

01:14.407 --> 01:17.827
The reason why it sounded like an excuse

01:17.911 --> 01:21.372
A weakness that draws in a fleeting future

01:21.456 --> 01:26.586
You mistake it for strength

01:27.962 --> 01:29.798
So detestable, so detestable

01:29.881 --> 01:31.549
So disgraceful, so disgraceful

01:31.633 --> 01:34.928
The heart that is so bleak

01:35.011 --> 01:36.805
So dark, so dark

01:36.888 --> 01:38.765
That it almost hides the moon

01:38.848 --> 01:42.352
If only you weren't here

01:42.435 --> 01:45.939
It sways and sways

01:46.022 --> 01:49.567
Carrying on its intentions
Just like a flower

01:49.651 --> 01:52.946
Taking it all away, taking it all away

01:53.029 --> 01:56.449
It tears the heart just like a storm would

01:56.533 --> 02:00.036
To you who is ignorant of
What eternity means

02:00.120 --> 02:03.581
It's time to show you the answer

02:03.665 --> 02:08.962
Beyond the endless spiral

02:09.045 --> 02:13.174
Who awaits there

02:16.219 --> 02:21.015
EPISODE 4:
IT MAKES YOU SMILE

02:21.724 --> 02:23.768
Even if you get hit, move quickly.

02:24.435 --> 02:26.229
Get back to your stance immediately.

02:26.312 --> 02:28.690
A HEART THAT IS UNBLEMISHED AND CLEAR

02:34.779 --> 02:36.573
Keep up with me.

02:47.333 --> 02:49.544
You died again.

02:50.461 --> 02:54.132
Remember, don't stop
even if someone gets killed.

02:59.178 --> 03:01.639
Once you stop, you'll also get killed.

03:06.728 --> 03:09.022
Tanjiro! I've been waiting for you.

03:09.856 --> 03:11.149
You seem well.

03:12.275 --> 03:15.028
You guys are useless!

03:15.111 --> 03:17.655
I hope you get eaten by demons and die!

03:18.323 --> 03:19.574
This crow again.

03:19.657 --> 03:22.201
What are you looking at? You small fries!

03:22.285 --> 03:27.457
It's Tokito's Kasugai Crow.
She's as rude as always.

03:28.041 --> 03:29.375
You're annoying.

03:29.459 --> 03:30.501
Shoo! Shoo!

03:30.585 --> 03:32.712
Huh? Shut up!

03:32.795 --> 03:34.464
I'll peck your eyeballs out!

03:34.547 --> 03:37.300
Oh, Tokito, long time no see.

03:37.383 --> 03:39.594
I look forward to training with you.

03:40.595 --> 03:42.597
Likewise, Tanjiro.

03:43.473 --> 03:44.891
Follow me for a moment.

03:45.683 --> 03:48.144
Be mindful and save water!

03:48.228 --> 03:49.687
You're annoying!

03:49.771 --> 03:50.813
What?

03:52.649 --> 03:53.733
I'm coming in.

03:54.859 --> 03:56.486
If it isn't Sir Tokito.

03:57.487 --> 03:58.655
Kanamori?

03:59.614 --> 04:02.867
Oh! You're here too, Tanjiro?

04:02.951 --> 04:06.579
Looks like you've now recovered.
It's good to see you.

04:06.663 --> 04:08.164
Yes, thank you.

04:09.040 --> 04:10.333
But why are you here?

04:11.125 --> 04:12.919
It was me who called him.

04:16.589 --> 04:18.925
Tanjiro, can you hold this for me?

04:24.389 --> 04:27.183
Step back a bit
and point the blade this way.

04:28.643 --> 04:29.727
Like this?

04:31.271 --> 04:32.897
Keep at it.

04:42.907 --> 04:43.950
How is it?

04:45.952 --> 04:47.662
It's so sharp!

04:48.788 --> 04:51.374
That's the reason I called Kanamori here.

04:52.625 --> 04:55.086
So, you're here to…

04:55.169 --> 04:59.132
Right. I'm staying permanently
to take care of his sword.

05:00.216 --> 05:04.804
I want my sword always in
the best condition for upcoming battles.

05:05.722 --> 05:10.393
When I told the Master that,
he said I could do as I pleased.

05:11.853 --> 05:13.313
The Master…

05:14.314 --> 05:18.192
And he even provided a place
specifically for sharpening swords.

05:19.652 --> 05:23.614
I wish he would pay attention
to his own health.

05:25.616 --> 05:29.120
He always prioritizes us the most.

05:30.621 --> 05:32.582
We can't thank him enough.

05:42.258 --> 05:43.801
Too many openings.

05:43.885 --> 05:45.470
Pick up your wooden sword.

05:58.232 --> 06:02.528
Do you think you can defeat your opponent
if you attack based on emotions?

06:03.237 --> 06:06.449
If anything, you'd be like
a moth flying into the fire.

06:07.867 --> 06:11.120
There are no do-overs
in a fight against the demons.

06:11.204 --> 06:15.666
Even if you win nine times and lose once,
that one loss costs you your life.

06:16.709 --> 06:21.464
You must hone every single move
to survive.

06:25.051 --> 06:26.928
Let's call it for today.

06:30.890 --> 06:32.016
Are you okay?

06:32.100 --> 06:33.309
You hurt?

06:35.311 --> 06:41.275
Hey, Kamado. Can you ask him
to ease up on the training a bit?

06:41.943 --> 06:45.363
At this rate, we'll collapse
before we even get to fight any demons.

06:46.781 --> 06:51.619
But I think Tokito
is the one having it the hardest.

06:52.453 --> 06:56.374
You see, he's been training us alone
this whole time.

06:57.208 --> 06:58.251
Makes sense.

06:58.334 --> 06:59.377
Right?

07:03.089 --> 07:04.423
Need a hand towel?

07:05.258 --> 07:06.342
Thank you.

07:06.425 --> 07:10.096
If only he could soften the way he speaks.

07:10.179 --> 07:12.348
His words cut really deep.

07:12.432 --> 07:13.683
Yeah, totally.

07:14.559 --> 07:18.938
Actually, I feel his tone has softened
compared to before.

07:19.647 --> 07:20.815
For real?

07:20.898 --> 07:22.150
It's over for us.

07:25.445 --> 07:26.487
Tokito?

07:27.447 --> 07:28.698
Where is he going?

07:30.074 --> 07:32.785
He always goes out somewhere at night.

07:33.369 --> 07:35.455
Maybe he's having dinner?

08:18.289 --> 08:20.958
FOUR

08:40.853 --> 08:44.440
Wind Breathing, Fourth Form:

08:45.566 --> 08:47.818
Rising Dust Storm!

08:48.361 --> 08:51.197
Serpent Breathing, Fifth Form:

08:51.697 --> 08:53.449
Slithering Serpent.

08:59.247 --> 09:00.414
We're evenly matched.

09:00.498 --> 09:01.958
Seems so.

09:04.710 --> 09:06.671
Let me join too.

09:07.755 --> 09:09.048
Tokito?

09:10.049 --> 09:13.052
You come all the way out here every day.

09:13.803 --> 09:16.305
Is your training during the day
doing fine?

09:16.847 --> 09:20.059
The training might be enough
for the other members,

09:20.142 --> 09:22.103
but not for me.

09:23.229 --> 09:24.480
Understandable.

09:24.564 --> 09:28.943
For us, this is the real Hashira Training.

09:29.944 --> 09:32.947
That's it. It's unfair
only the two of you get to do it.

09:33.864 --> 09:37.285
All right, in honor of your coming,

09:37.368 --> 09:41.664
Shinazugawa and I
will take you on together.

09:42.832 --> 09:43.958
Let's get started.

09:44.041 --> 09:46.961
Both of you against me? How unfair.

09:47.837 --> 09:50.381
Anytime, I'm ready!

10:07.481 --> 10:10.109
Good! Beat them both!

10:10.192 --> 10:12.486
You're the best!

10:12.570 --> 10:13.654
Shut up!

10:18.034 --> 10:19.994
Today's training really hit hard.

10:20.828 --> 10:24.665
If I let my guard down even a little,
I might get seriously injured.

10:25.249 --> 10:28.753
Otherwise, there's no point in training.

10:29.462 --> 10:31.964
During the day,
sparring with the other members.

10:32.048 --> 10:34.925
And at night,
real combat training with you guys.

10:36.260 --> 10:37.595
Not bad.

10:38.888 --> 10:42.433
Tokito, how was your training today?

10:43.768 --> 10:46.103
Tanjiro came to my place today.

10:47.229 --> 10:50.775
That guy, huh?
So he's still hanging in there.

10:51.692 --> 10:53.903
His wounds seem to be healing.

10:54.612 --> 10:58.866
Maybe he'll be fully recovered
by the time he comes to your place, Iguro.

11:00.242 --> 11:01.744
I see.

11:01.827 --> 11:05.831
That means I can go all out
to train him, then?

11:07.166 --> 11:09.627
Even if he's gotten a bit stronger,

11:09.710 --> 11:13.839
I'll show him that he's still
nowhere near Hashira's level.

11:14.882 --> 11:16.550
That sounds fun.

11:18.636 --> 11:20.846
Do your best, Tanjiro.

11:27.645 --> 11:29.105
There, you died.

11:32.066 --> 11:33.901
You stopped moving.

11:36.695 --> 11:38.697
There, you also died.

11:45.454 --> 11:48.207
It seems there's not enough tension.

11:49.500 --> 11:52.420
How about using real swords?

11:54.922 --> 11:56.298
Bring the real swords.

11:56.966 --> 11:58.259
Okay!

12:03.556 --> 12:05.641
Let's begin.

12:07.435 --> 12:08.853
But…

12:09.562 --> 12:10.688
Take your stance.

12:11.939 --> 12:13.941
I can't… I can't do it.

12:15.359 --> 12:16.444
Come on.

12:37.298 --> 12:39.508
-Tokito, if you continue--
-I'm sorry!

12:52.521 --> 12:56.108
You didn't attack recklessly.
Consider that progress.

12:59.069 --> 13:00.196
I understand.

13:01.071 --> 13:02.615
Compared to you,

13:02.698 --> 13:06.118
I can't possibly comprehend
how hard to fight in a battle.

13:06.202 --> 13:09.788
I know that you go somewhere every night

13:09.872 --> 13:13.000
and return covered in bruises
beneath your clothes.

13:14.084 --> 13:17.338
I saw you bathing your wounds at dawn.

13:18.756 --> 13:21.634
We'll work harder, so…

13:25.221 --> 13:27.306
You're doing good in your own way.

13:28.307 --> 13:30.809
But that doesn't guarantee victory.

13:32.436 --> 13:35.940
I don't want you guys
to be killed by demons.

13:38.275 --> 13:40.861
I want all of you to live long
if possible.

13:41.737 --> 13:43.531
That's what I really hope for.

13:44.949 --> 13:46.200
Tokito…

13:51.997 --> 13:55.251
Good, Tanjiro. You're faster than before.

14:01.298 --> 14:05.511
Make your muscles' transition
between tense and relaxed even smoother.

14:08.180 --> 14:09.223
Good!

14:12.601 --> 14:14.186
Yes, like that!

14:16.021 --> 14:18.816
If you do so,
your stamina will last longer.

14:32.162 --> 14:35.207
The movement of your legs and hips
flows perfectly.

14:36.417 --> 14:39.420
You can go to the next Hashira, Tanjiro.

14:40.212 --> 14:42.256
Already?

14:42.339 --> 14:43.382
Yes.

14:43.465 --> 14:45.593
I've only been here for five days.

14:45.676 --> 14:49.138
Because you're doing everything
exactly as I told you to.

14:51.390 --> 14:53.934
That means, we also…

14:54.018 --> 14:56.103
We've been here for two weeks.

14:56.896 --> 15:00.316
What are you talking about?
You guys are still not doing well.

15:00.399 --> 15:02.192
After practicing swinging the sword,

15:02.276 --> 15:05.905
you guys need to train in striking
until the practice dummy breaks.

15:08.824 --> 15:10.743
What a difference in treatment.

15:14.788 --> 15:15.956
Tokito!

15:17.499 --> 15:20.210
Let's have a paper airplane
flying competition!

15:21.086 --> 15:22.922
Why suddenly?

15:23.631 --> 15:25.215
Ta-da!

15:25.716 --> 15:28.719
I heard you like paper airplanes.

15:29.720 --> 15:32.389
If that's the case,
I can give it a shot too.

15:33.057 --> 15:35.643
Sir Tokito's hobby, huh?

15:35.726 --> 15:37.394
Let me think.

15:38.062 --> 15:42.232
Well, if there's one,
it'd be making paper airplanes.

15:43.192 --> 15:44.693
Paper airplanes?

15:44.777 --> 15:47.571
Yes, I have plenty of them over there.

15:50.449 --> 15:55.704
If I win, you must talk a bit more gently
towards the other members.

15:56.455 --> 15:57.831
How about that?

16:00.918 --> 16:02.419
Yeah, sure.

16:03.420 --> 16:04.380
I won't lose.

16:05.172 --> 16:06.757
You can't win against me.

16:08.050 --> 16:10.302
You're a good guy.

16:14.348 --> 16:15.474
Are you sure?

16:15.557 --> 16:19.603
It's my win if mine can fly longer
one out of ten tries?

16:20.354 --> 16:24.400
Yeah. Though you'll never win
against me anyway.

16:24.483 --> 16:26.568
If it's one out of ten…

16:26.652 --> 16:28.696
Do you accept or not?

16:28.779 --> 16:30.155
Of course, I accept!

16:30.948 --> 16:34.952
Then, throw it at the same time
on my signal!

16:35.786 --> 16:38.664
One! Two! Three!

16:39.415 --> 16:40.541
Throw!

16:42.167 --> 16:43.210
Huh?

16:43.293 --> 16:45.546
It's Sir Tokito's victory!

16:45.629 --> 16:47.172
You can do it, Kamado!

16:47.256 --> 16:48.882
You still have a chance!

16:48.966 --> 16:50.009
Throw!

16:52.469 --> 16:54.638
It's Sir Tokito's victory!

16:54.722 --> 16:55.848
Throw!

16:57.641 --> 17:00.644
It's… It's Sir Tokito's victory.

17:00.728 --> 17:01.729
Throw!

17:05.482 --> 17:07.317
It's Sir Tokito's victory.

17:08.068 --> 17:11.697
One more chance.

17:12.531 --> 17:14.158
Don't give up, Tanjiro!

17:14.241 --> 17:17.327
Yeah, I only need to win once.

17:20.873 --> 17:22.332
I lost.

17:22.416 --> 17:23.625
DEFEAT

17:24.251 --> 17:27.129
I told you, didn't I? You can't win.

17:28.380 --> 17:31.592
I thought I could win at least once.

17:31.675 --> 17:32.968
Hashira!

17:33.052 --> 17:35.471
May I join the challenge as well?

17:35.554 --> 17:37.765
I'm good with throwing paper airplanes.

17:37.848 --> 17:40.768
Me too!
I've been the best in my village before.

17:40.851 --> 17:44.688
Hey, I won first place
in my town's paper airplane contest!

17:44.772 --> 17:45.773
Let's do it then!

17:45.856 --> 17:47.024
I'm in!

17:47.107 --> 17:48.984
Someone, get us lots of paper!

17:57.993 --> 18:00.079
Can I watch for a bit?

18:06.543 --> 18:07.836
This time, I'll win.

18:09.713 --> 18:11.340
What are you doing, Ugly?

18:11.423 --> 18:12.758
Look at you, you small fry!

18:12.841 --> 18:13.926
You're annoying!

18:14.009 --> 18:15.761
I'm not!

18:17.304 --> 18:18.972
Are you ready, everyone?

18:19.056 --> 18:20.265
Yeah!

18:22.017 --> 18:23.769
Let's throw!

19:27.666 --> 19:32.421
It's probably true that Muzan Kibutsuji
is targeting Nezuko

19:32.504 --> 19:34.464
because she has overcome the sun.

19:34.548 --> 19:37.301
Also, we rarely encounter demons
these days.

19:38.177 --> 19:41.680
Thanks to that, we can focus
on the Hashira Training.

19:42.806 --> 19:45.684
I was worried about
being separated from Nezuko.

19:45.767 --> 19:50.022
But if I bring her to my mission,
that would play right into enemy hands.

19:50.105 --> 19:51.481
It's too dangerous.

19:53.108 --> 19:56.737
It's also possible that Kibutsuji
is gathering his demons to capture Nezuko,

19:56.820 --> 19:59.448
so that he can end up hiding.

20:01.408 --> 20:04.369
I'll train hard,
become stronger than ever,

20:04.453 --> 20:06.079
and go to get Nezuko later.

20:09.124 --> 20:11.418
You're always so positive, Tanjiro.

20:19.092 --> 20:24.681
Because right now, Nezuko has someone
I really trust with her.

20:31.730 --> 20:32.856
Tanjiro.

20:34.983 --> 20:38.487
We must defeat Kibutsuji together
with everyone.

20:52.000 --> 20:56.296
The flame that burns heaven

20:56.380 --> 21:03.345
Truer than the truth

21:03.428 --> 21:07.391
The voice of prayers and
The sounds of shouting

21:07.474 --> 21:14.022
Are fleeting like winged insects

21:14.106 --> 21:18.652
Why do those who devour lives

21:18.735 --> 21:25.617
Beg mercy as if not knowing impurity

21:25.701 --> 21:31.790
Those souls that win through
The darkness can only reach

21:31.873 --> 21:36.586
Obtain that eternity

21:36.670 --> 21:42.301
There's a feeling here
That doesn't know demise

21:42.384 --> 21:47.514
Speak your dream, you strong one

21:47.597 --> 21:53.270
A resound congratulating tune of eternity

21:53.353 --> 21:59.026
Into the light that governs the sky

21:59.109 --> 22:03.238
In the corner of the world that is messy

22:03.322 --> 22:07.534
A blade of a sword
That still wriggles and resists

22:07.617 --> 22:13.415
Grovels and struggles miserably

22:19.463 --> 22:22.257
Tanjiro! Long time no see!

22:22.341 --> 22:24.384
Welcome to my mansion!

22:24.468 --> 22:26.094
It's been a while!

22:26.178 --> 22:28.013
Glad to see you looking well!

22:28.096 --> 22:29.723
You too, Tanjiro.

22:30.390 --> 22:32.184
Do you keep bees?

22:33.643 --> 22:36.063
I smell the sweet scent of honey.

22:36.146 --> 22:38.190
Oh! You knew?

22:38.273 --> 22:40.192
That's right!

22:40.275 --> 22:46.615
Honeycomb on bread
is super-duper delicious!

22:46.698 --> 22:49.242
And smear a lot of butter too!

22:49.326 --> 22:51.745
I'll brew some black tea at 3:00!

22:51.828 --> 22:54.414
I'll make pancakes too!
So look forward to it!

22:55.290 --> 23:00.337
Butter? Pancakes?
And I barely know black tea.

23:00.420 --> 23:05.050
Sweets! Bread! Pancakes!

23:05.926 --> 23:06.760
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA:
HASHIRA TRAINING ARC NO. 4

23:07.719 --> 23:10.222
This time I'll tell you about Tokito.

23:10.305 --> 23:14.559
I'm looking forward to it because I feel
I haven't remembered everything.

23:15.435 --> 23:18.230
Here we go, the Taisho period secret.

23:18.313 --> 23:20.107
Since before he joined the Corps,

23:20.190 --> 23:25.612
he had nerves of steel that he could
sleep through storms and lightning.

23:25.695 --> 23:28.698
It sounds like I'm some kind
of insensitive person.

23:28.782 --> 23:31.284
And you never lost your appetite either.

23:31.952 --> 23:36.414
But while I had lost my memories,
my personality was like my brother's.

23:36.498 --> 23:39.751
That made me happy,
as if he was protecting me.

23:39.835 --> 23:41.128
Tokito…

23:41.837 --> 23:44.589
Next up on Episode 5:
"I Even Ate a Demon."

23:44.673 --> 23:45.966
TO BE CONTINUED
